1.
First clarify the requirements
Before writing any class, ask questions.

For a vending machine :-

Products
 What types of products can it sell?
 Does every product have a different price?
 Can multiple products have the same type?
 Do products have an expiry date?

Inventory
    How many products can each slot hold?
    What happens when a product is out of stock?
    Can an administrator refill the machine?

Payment
    What payment methods are supported? :- Cash? Card? UPI?
    Can the user insert money in multiple steps?
    Can the machine return change?
    What happens if insufficient money is inserted?

Transaction
     Can the user cancel?
     Should inserted money be refunded?
     What happens if the machine runs out of change?
     What happens if dispensing fails?

Admin
    Do we need an admin interface?
    Can an admin add/remove products?
    Can an admin collect money?

For an interview, you could say :-

I'll assume the machine supports multiple products, cash payment, inventory management, 
cancellation, and change return.
I'll keep card/UPI and admin operations extensible but won't implement them unless required.

