Payment -> interface
PricingStrategy -> HourlyPricing , FlatPricing , WeekendPricing
                   This demonstrates Strategy.
Vehicle -> Car , Bike , Truck
ParkingTicket -> Vehicle enter -> ParkingTicket -> Vehicle exits -> Calculate fee
                 Ticket can contain : ticketId, vehicle, slot, entryTime, exitTime
ParkingSpotAllocationStrategy -> 
         interface SpotAllocationStrategy {
            ParkingSlot findSlot(Vehicle vehicle);
         }
    Implement :- NearestSlotStrategy
                 FirstAvailableStrategy
                 RandomSlotStrategy 
ParkingSlot -> NormalSlot
               EVSlot

ParkingLot ◆── 1..* Floor
Floor ◆── 1..* ParkingSlot.   This clearly demonstrates composition + multiplicity.

Concurrency
What if two cars simultaneously try to take the last available slot?

The operation of finding an available slot and marking it occupied needs to be atomic.
Otherwise, two threads could both see the last slot as available and assign it.
I would synchronize/lock the slot-allocation operation so that only one thread can allocate 
a particular slot at a time.

Edge cases

Be ready for:
   Parking lot full , Vehicle already parked , Vehicle exits without a valid ticket ,
   Payment failure , No compatible slot , Invalid ticket


