}

Balance Tracking

class BalanceManager{
      private Map<User, Map<User, BigDecimal>> balances;
      void addExpense(Expense expense);
      void settle(User from, User to, BigDecimal amount);
      BigDecimal getBalance(User from, User to);  
}

Group
class Group {
       private String groupId;
       private String name;
       private List<User> members;
       private List<Expense> expenses;       
}

SplitwiseService
I don't want User, Expense, and Group coordinating everything themselves.

class SplitwiseService {
         private Map<String, User> users;
         private Map<String, Group> groups;
         private BalanceManager balanceManager;

         void addExpense(...);
         void addUserToGroup(...);
         void settleExpense(...);

         Map<User, BigDecimal> getBalances(User user);
}

Expense ◆── 1..* Split
Split ─── User because a split refers to a user.
Group ◆── Expense
Group ─── User

Concurrency
What happens if two users add expenses simultaneoulsy ?



Edge cases
-> Expense amount must be positive.
-> Exact split amounts must equal total expense.
-> Percentage splits must total 100%.
-> User must belong to the group.
-> Cannot settle more than the outstanding debt.
-> Cannot add duplicate group members.
-> A user cannot split an expense with someone outside the allowed participants.
-> Handle money using BigDecimal/a money abstraction rather than double.

Alice -> SplitwiseService.addExpense() -> EqualSplit.calculateSplits() -> Expense created ->
BalanceManager.update() -> Bob owes Alice ₹300 , Charlie owes Alice ₹300


